<h1>Run provenance</h1>

<p>
  What each turn was actually told. The rules are pinned at the
  <strong>version</strong> they were injected at, so the exact instruction text is
  recoverable from the revision trail even after the rule has been edited — this is
  the difference between &ldquo;the agent probably followed policy&rdquo; and
  &ldquo;here is the policy that was in the prompt.&rdquo;
</p>

<p>
  The last two columns are <strong>not the same kind of thing.</strong>
  <em>Rules injected</em> is written by the engine from the rule set it rendered
  into the prompt: it is evidence of what the agent was told.
  <em>Rules the agent claims it applied</em> is a line the model wrote in its own
  reply — an <strong>unverified self-report, not proof the rule was followed.</strong>
  A model has been observed contradicting a rule while citing it, and that turn
  records exactly like a compliant one. Read a citation as &ldquo;the rule reached
  the model&rsquo;s attention,&rdquo; never as &ldquo;the rule held.&rdquo; Policy
  that has to hold belongs in a <code>guard</code> rule, which the engine checks
  itself.
</p>

<p>
  Neither column can tell you whether a rule <em>held</em> — a turn that complied
  and cited records identically to one that contradicted the rule and cited it
  anyway. The only thing that separates them is <strong>what the agent actually
  said</strong>, which lives in the host's own chat tables, not here. Open a run to
  read that turn's reply and check the claim against it.
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>When</th><th>Agent</th><th>Account</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Status</th>
      <th>Model</th><th>Tokens</th><th>Snapshot</th><th>Memories</th>
      <th>Rules injected <small>(engine — evidence)</small></th>
      <th>Rules the agent <em>claims</em> it applied <small>(unverified)</small></th>
      <th>What it said <small>(the check)</small></th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @runs.each do |run| %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= link_to run.created_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"), admin_run_path(run) %></td>
        <td><%= run.agent_slug %></td>
        <td><%= subject_label(run) %></td>
        <td><%= run.trigger %></td>
        <td><%= run.status %><%= " (#{run.error_class})" if run.error_class %></td>
        <td><%= run.model %></td>
        <td><%= run.total_tokens %></td>
        <td><code><%= run.snapshot_digest.to_s.first(12) %></code></td>
        <td><%= run.memory_ids.size %></td>
        <td>
          <% if run.rules.any? %>
            <ul>
              <% run.injected_rule_texts.each do |text| %>
                <li><%= text %></li>
              <% end %>
            </ul>
          <% else %>
            none
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <td>
          <% if run.rule_ids_applied.any? %>
            <%= run.rule_ids_applied.join(", ") %>
            <br><small>claimed, not verified</small>
          <% else %>
            —
          <% end %>
          <% if run.unknown_citations? %>
            <br><strong>cited but never injected: <%= run.unknown_rule_ids.join(", ") %></strong>
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <td>
          <% if run.message_id %>
            <%= link_to "read the reply", admin_run_path(run) %>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to "no reply recorded", admin_run_path(run) %>
          <% end %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>
